{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a light-driven cyclic reaction network for the enantioselective synthesis of amines from cyclic imines. It combines a photoredox-catalyzed reduction step using a water-soluble iridium photosensitizer (Na3[Ir(sppy)3]) and ascorbic acid as a HAT donor with an enzymatic re-oxidation step using monoamine oxidase (MAO-N-9). This concurrent process leads to the accumulation of enantioenriched (R)-amines in aqueous solution.",
